PART A.2 -- RESONANCE / TRANSFER-OPERATOR RECONSTRUCTION (P2).
  e(E) = sum_{s!=0} INT Hhat_s(x) e(2pi i sMx) dx.  e(2pi i sMx) = L_M[e(2pi i sx)].
  Reconstruct e(E) from truncated s-sum and compare to exact p0_exact - p0_decorr.
============================================================================================
  NOTE: the resonance integral INT Hhat_s(x) e(2pi i sMx) dx is highly oscillatory
  (frequency sM up to ~200); a plain Riemann sum at Nx converges slowly, so the
  RECONSTRUCTED e is a crude majorant of the exact e. The point of this part is only
  to confirm (i) the s=+-1 harmonic dominates and (ii) per-|s| magnitudes fall ~1/|s|.

